IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-schedules`
IMPORT `voca-core`
IMPORT `voca-seat-levy`

-- Cases for the seat of the person on whom the s 61 levy is imposed (voca-seat-levy.l4). Every expected value was
-- worked by hand from the deposited Act (REPV014, s 61 as in force from 1 July 2025) and Regulations (REPV014R1, reg
-- 26), never copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comment above each assertion. HYPOTHETICAL
-- people throughout. The value of a revenue unit is not deposited: every case uses a HYPOTHETICAL $1.25.
--
-- Argument order of the levy question: how the offence was dealt with; the law it was against; a local council
-- prosecuted me; adult, child or body corporate; prosecuted on indictment; the value of a revenue unit.

`one revenue unit` MEANS 1.25

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. Infringement notices and enforcement orders (s 61(2)(b), (c), (6); reg 26(b)).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Sam, an adult, pays a speeding infringement notice: 40 revenue units (s 61(6)(a)), 40 x 1.25 = $50.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `expiated by paying the amount in an infringement notice` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 40 50
-- Sam pays a parking infringement notice under Part 12 of the Australian Road Rules: no levy (reg 26(b)).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `expiated by paying the amount in an infringement notice` `Part 12 of the Australian Road Rules` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `reg 26(b): no levy on a person issued a notice under that law to pay a prescribed amount instead of a penalty`
-- A litter infringement notice (the Litter Act 1972): no levy (reg 26(b)).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `expiated by paying the amount in an infringement notice` `the Litter Act 1972` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `reg 26(b): no levy on a person issued a notice under that law to pay a prescribed amount instead of a penalty`
-- A child of 16 pays a speeding notice: s 61(6) does not vary with age, 40 units, $50.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `expiated by paying the amount in an infringement notice` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `a child` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 40 50
-- Sam does not pay a speeding notice and an enforcement order is made: 40 units, $50 (s 61(2)(c), (6)).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `an enforcement order was made` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 40 50
-- An enforcement order for an unpaid parking notice: READING, reg 26(b) reaches the person issued that notice: no levy.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `an enforcement order was made` `Part 12 of the Australian Road Rules` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `reg 26(b): no levy on a person issued a notice under that law to pay a prescribed amount instead of a penalty`
-- The council question answered yes for a paid notice: reg 26(c) needs "a person found guilty", so it does not apply;
-- 40 units, $50.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `expiated by paying the amount in an infringement notice` `another law in force in the Territory` TRUE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 40 50

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. Found guilty (s 61(2)(a), (3); reg 26(a), (c)).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Jo, an adult, is found guilty of a summary offence and fined: 150 units (s 61(3)(a)(ii)), 150 x 1.25 = $187.50.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 150 187.5
-- Prosecuted on indictment, a fine and a bond: 200 units (s 61(3)(a)(i)), $250.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `an adult` TRUE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 200 250
-- Imprisoned for the offence: no levy under s 61(2)(a).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and imprisoned for the offence` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `an adult` TRUE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `s 61(2)(a): the levy on a person found guilty applies only if they are not imprisoned for the offence`
-- A child found guilty: 50 units (s 61(3)(b)), $62.50. Prosecuted on indictment changes nothing for a child.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `a child` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 50 62.5
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `a child` TRUE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 50 62.5
-- Jo's company found guilty: 1 000 units (s 61(3)(c)), $1 250.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `another law in force in the Territory` FALSE `a body corporate` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `a levy is imposed, which a court must not reduce (s 61(9))` 1000 1250
-- Found guilty of an offence against the Return to Work Act 1986, or the Litter Act 1972: no levy (reg 26(a)).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `the Return to Work Act 1986` FALSE `a body corporate` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `reg 26(a): no levy on a person found guilty of an offence against that law`
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `the Litter Act 1972` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `reg 26(a): no levy on a person found guilty of an offence against that law`
-- Found guilty on a council's prosecution of an offence against another law: no levy (reg 26(c)).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `another law in force in the Territory` TRUE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `reg 26(c): no levy on a person found guilty of an offence prosecuted by a local government council`
-- A council by-law, prosecuted by the council: (a) and (c) both apply; the answer names (a).
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `a by-law of a local government council` TRUE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `reg 26(a): no levy on a person found guilty of an offence against that law`
-- An offence against a law not in force in the Territory is not an "offence" (s 61(10)): no levy.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the victims levy` `found guilty and not imprisoned for the offence` `a law not in force in the Territory` FALSE `an adult` FALSE `one revenue unit` EQUALS `no levy` `s 61(10): it is not an offence against a law in force in the Territory`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. Part payments (s 61(8)) and immunity (s 61(7)). Sam's speeding notice: $300, with the $50 levy.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Sam pays $30: all of it to the levy, nothing to the notice. Pays $100: $50 to the levy, $50 to the notice. Pays $350:
-- $50 and $300. The levy already paid ($0 owing), pays $100: $0 and $100.
#ASSERT `How much of my payment goes to the levy` 30 50 EQUALS `of the payment, in dollars, this goes to the levy and this to the infringement notice amount` 30 0
#ASSERT `How much of my payment goes to the levy` 100 50 EQUALS `of the payment, in dollars, this goes to the levy and this to the infringement notice amount` 50 50
#ASSERT `How much of my payment goes to the levy` 350 50 EQUALS `of the payment, in dollars, this goes to the levy and this to the infringement notice amount` 50 300
#ASSERT `How much of my payment goes to the levy` 100 0 EQUALS `of the payment, in dollars, this goes to the levy and this to the infringement notice amount` 0 100
-- Sam has paid $300 in all: $350 is due (the $300 in the notice and the $50 levy), so not immune until $50 more is
-- paid. Paid $350: s 61(7) is met.
#ASSERT `Have I paid enough for immunity from prosecution` 300 50 300 EQUALS `not immune from prosecution (s 61(7)) until this much more, in dollars, is paid` 50
#ASSERT `Have I paid enough for immunity from prosecution` 300 50 350 EQUALS `s 61(7) is met: the amount in the notice or order and the levy are both paid`
-- A parking notice of $80, no levy (reg 26(b)): $80 paid meets s 61(7).
#ASSERT `Have I paid enough for immunity from prosecution` 80 0 80 EQUALS `s 61(7) is met: the amount in the notice or order and the levy are both paid`
